"S"},{"fullName":"Natha S","lastName":"Natha","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Simpson H","lastName":"Simpson","firstName":"H","initials":"H"},{"fullName":"Ramtoola S","lastName":"Ramtoola","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Hutchesson A","lastName":"Hutchesson","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Fleming S","lastName":"Fleming","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Tan GD","lastName":"Tan","firstName":"G D","initials":"GD"},{"fullName":"MacLeod K","lastName":"MacLeod","firstName":"K","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Brand C","lastName":"Brand","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Broadbent D","lastName":"Broadbent","firstName":"D","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Vora J","lastName":"Vora","firstName":"J","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Bhatnagar D","lastName":"Bhatnagar","firstName":"D","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Mishra B","lastName":"Mishra","firstName":"B","initials":"B"},{"fullName":"Reckless J","lastName":"Reckless","firstName":"J","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Hughes E","lastName":"Hughes","firstName":"E","initials":"E"},{"fullName":"Robertson D","lastName":"Robertson","firstName":"D","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Thomas C","lastName":"Thomas","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Hyer S","lastName":"Hyer","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Rodin A","lastName":"Rodin","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Gilbey S","lastName":"Gilbey","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Gable D","lastName":"Gable","firstName":"D","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Baxter M","lastName":"Baxter","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Hale P","lastName":"Hale","firstName":"P","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Kong N","lastName":"Kong","firstName":"N","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Burrows G","lastName":"Burrows","firstName":"G","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Chowdhury T","lastName":"Chowdhury","firstName":"T","initials":"T"},{"fullName":"Peterson D","lastName":"Peterson","firstName":"D","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Paisey R","lastName":"Paisey","firstName":"R","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Chattington P","lastName":"Chattington","firstName":"P","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Clements M","lastName":"Clements","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Singhal P","lastName":"Singhal","firstName":"P","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Jafree A","lastName":"Jafree","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Williams C","lastName":"Williams","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Caldwell G","lastName":"Caldwell","firstName":"G","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Signy M","lastName":"Signy","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Gallen I","lastName":"Gallen","firstName":"I","initials":"I"},{"fullName":"Jennings P","lastName":"Jennings","firstName":"P","initials":"P"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5909-4265"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7284-4673"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8969-371X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1179-0023"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6170-4402"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0374-8519"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0971-3026"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4956-4512"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"16","volume":"379","journalIssueId":2739972,"dateOfPublication":"2018 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2018,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"N Engl J Med","title":"The New England journal of medicine","essn":"1533-4406","issn":"0028-4793","nlmid":"0255562","isoabbreviation":"N Engl J Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2018-10-01"},"pubYear":"2018","pageInfo":"1540-1550","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Increased intake of n-3 fatty acids has been associated with a reduced risk of cardiovascular disease in observational studies, but this finding has not been confirmed in randomized trials. It remains unclear whether n-3 (also called omega-3) fatty acid supplementation has cardiovascular benefit in patients with diabetes mellitus.<h4>Methods</h4>We randomly assigned 15,480 patients with diabetes but without evidence of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease to receive 1-g capsules containing either n-3 fatty acids (fatty acid group) or matching placebo (olive oil) daily. The primary outcome was a first serious vascular event (i.e., nonfatal myocardial infarction or stroke, transient ischemic attack, or vascular death, excluding confirmed intracranial hemorrhage). The secondary outcome was a first serious vascular event or any arterial revascularization.<h4>Results</h4>During a mean follow-up of 7.4 years (adherence rate, 76%), a serious vascular event occurred in 689 patients (8.9%) in the fatty acid group and in 712 (9.2%) in the placebo group (rate ratio, 0.97; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.87 to 1.08; P=0.55). The composite outcome of a serious vascular event or revascularization occurred in 882 patients (11.4%) and 887 patients (11.5%), respectively (rate ratio, 1.00; 95% CI, 0.91 to 1.09). Death from any cause occurred in 752 patients (9.7%) in the fatty acid group and in 788 (10.2%) in the placebo group (rate ratio, 0.95; 95% CI, 0.86 to 1.05). There were no significant between-group differences in the rates of nonfatal serious adverse events.<h4>Conclusions</h4>Among patients with diabetes without evidence of cardiovascular disease, there was no significant difference in the risk of serious vascular events between those who were assigned to receive n-3 fatty acid supplementation and those who were assigned to receive placebo. (Funded by the British Heart Foundation and others; Current Controlled Trials number, ISRCTN60635500 ; ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT00135226 .).","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Medical Research Council","acronym":"MRC_","grantId":"MC_U137686